{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"VERY IMPORTANT: This utility is currently in an experimental stage. This means that breaking changes will happen in minor AND patch releases. Use at your own risk. If you choose to rely on this in production in an experimental stage, please lock your version to a patch-level version to avoid unexpected breakages."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"broadcastQueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" is a utility for broadcasting and syncing the state of your queryClient between browser tabs/windows with the same origin."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This utility comes as a separate package and is available under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'@tanstack/query-broadcast-client-experimental'"},{"type":"text","value":" import."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"broadcastQueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" function, and pass it your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" instance, and optionally, set a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"broadcastChannel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { broadcastQueryClient } from '@tanstack/query-broadcast-client-experimental'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nbroadcastQueryClient({\n  queryClient,\n  broadcastChannel: 'my-app',\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"broadcastqueryclient","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"broadcastQueryClient"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass this function a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" instance and optionally, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"broadcastChannel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"broadcastQueryClient({ queryClient, broadcastChannel })","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An object of options:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface BroadcastQueryClientOptions {\n  /** The QueryClient to sync */\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n  /** This is the unique channel name that will be used\n   * to communicate between tabs and windows */\n  broadcastChannel?: string\n  /** Options for the BroadcastChannel API */\n  options?: BroadcastChannelOptions\n  /**\n   * Called when a query event fails to broadcast to other tabs — most\n   * commonly because the query's data, error, or key contains a value the\n   * structured-clone algorithm cannot serialize (e.g. `ReadableStream`,\n   * `File`, functions, Vue `reactive` proxies).\n   *\n   * If omitted, a `console.warn` is emitted in development so failures\n   * are never entirely silent. May return a `Promise`; any rejection is\n   * caught internally.\n   */\n  onBroadcastError?: (\n    error: unknown,\n    event: BroadcastErrorEvent,\n  ) => void | Promise<void>\n}\n\ninterface BroadcastErrorEvent {\n  type: 'updated' | 'removed' | 'added'\n  queryHash: string\n  queryKey: QueryKey\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default options are:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  broadcastChannel = 'tanstack-query',\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"handling-broadcast-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handling broadcast errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If your cache can hold values that are not structured-cloneable — such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReadableStream"},{"type":"text","value":" (from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response.body"},{"type":"text","value":", streaming APIs, or AI SDKs), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":", functions, or framework proxies like Vue "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactive"},{"type":"text","value":" — the underlying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BroadcastChannel.postMessage"},{"type":"text","value":" call will reject for that query. Cross-tab sync is skipped for that query; the rest of the cache continues to broadcast normally."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.warn"},{"type":"text","value":" is emitted in development so failures are never silent. Provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBroadcastError"},{"type":"text","value":" to route failures to your own error tracker:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import * as Sentry from '@sentry/browser'\nimport { broadcastQueryClient } from '@tanstack/query-broadcast-client-experimental'\n\nbroadcastQueryClient({\n  queryClient,\n  broadcastChannel: 'my-app',\n  onBroadcastError: (error, event) => {\n    Sentry.captureException(error, {\n      tags: { broadcastEvent: event.type },\n      extra: { queryHash: event.queryHash, queryKey: event.queryKey },\n    })\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"api","text":"API","level":2},{"id":"broadcastqueryclient","text":"broadcastQueryClient","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"handling-broadcast-errors","text":"Handling broadcast errors","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> VERY IMPORTANT: This utility is currently in an experimental stage. This means that breaking changes will happen in minor AND patch releases. Use at your own risk. If you choose to rely on this in production in an experimental stage, please lock your version to a patch-level version to avoid unexpected breakages.\n\n`broadcastQueryClient` is a utility for broadcasting and syncing the state of your queryClient between browser tabs/windows with the same origin.\n\n## Installation\n\nThis utility comes as a separate package and is available under the `'@tanstack/query-broadcast-client-experimental'` import.\n\n## Usage\n\nImport the `broadcastQueryClient` function, and pass it your `QueryClient` instance, and optionally, set a `broadcastChannel`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { broadcastQueryClient } from '@tanstack/query-broadcast-client-experimental'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nbroadcastQueryClient({\n  queryClient,\n  broadcastChannel: 'my-app',\n})\n```\n\n## API\n\n### `broadcastQueryClient`\n\nPass this function a `QueryClient` instance and optionally, a `broadcastChannel`.\n\n```tsx\nbroadcastQueryClient({ queryClient, broadcastChannel })\n```\n\n### `Options`\n\nAn object of options:\n\n```tsx\ninterface BroadcastQueryClientOptions {\n  /** The QueryClient to sync */\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n  /** This is the unique channel name that will be used\n   * to communicate between tabs and windows */\n  broadcastChannel?: string\n  /** Options for the BroadcastChannel API */\n  options?: BroadcastChannelOptions\n  /**\n   * Called when a query event fails to broadcast to other tabs — most\n   * commonly because the query's data, error, or key contains a value the\n   * structured-clone algorithm cannot serialize (e.g. `ReadableStream`,\n   * `File`, functions, Vue `reactive` proxies).\n   *\n   * If omitted, a `console.warn` is emitted in development so failures\n   * are never entirely silent. May return a `Promise`; any rejection is\n   * caught internally.\n   */\n  onBroadcastError?: (\n    error: unknown,\n    event: BroadcastErrorEvent,\n  ) => void | Promise<void>\n}\n\ninterface BroadcastErrorEvent {\n  type: 'updated' | 'removed' | 'added'\n  queryHash: string\n  queryKey: QueryKey\n}\n```\n\nThe default options are:\n\n```tsx\n{\n  broadcastChannel = 'tanstack-query',\n}\n```\n\n## Handling broadcast errors\n\nIf your cache can hold values that are not structured-cloneable — such as `ReadableStream` (from `Response.body`, streaming APIs, or AI SDKs), `File`, functions, or framework proxies like Vue `reactive` — the underlying `BroadcastChannel.postMessage` call will reject for that query. Cross-tab sync is skipped for that query; the rest of the cache continues to broadcast normally.\n\nBy default, a `console.warn` is emitted in development so failures are never silent. Provide `onBroadcastError` to route failures to your own error tracker:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as Sentry from '@sentry/browser'\nimport { broadcastQueryClient } from '@tanstack/query-broadcast-client-experimental'\n\nbroadcastQueryClient({\n  queryClient,\n  broadcastChannel: 'my-app',\n  onBroadcastError: (error, event) => {\n    Sentry.captureException(error, {\n      tags: { broadcastEvent: event.type },\n      extra: { queryHash: event.queryHash, queryKey: event.queryKey },\n    })\n  },\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: broadcastQueryClient\ntitle: broadcastQueryClient (Experimental)\nref: docs/framework/react/plugins/broadcastQueryClient.md\n---\n"}
